<title>SINGAPORE: Jaya Holdings abandons Pakistan project.</title>
<headline>Jaya Holdings abandons Pakistan project.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jaya Holdings Ltd said on Tuesday it has ceased its Pakistan project with Far East Levingston on a 134 megawatt barge-mounted plant.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that despite exhaustive efforts by both companies to fulfil their obligations, &quot;the response and co-operation from the relevant Pakistani authorities have been unsatisfactory&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;The directors therefore do not deem it prudent to pursue this particular project any further,&quot; the company said. No details of the project's cost were given.</p>
<p>Jaya said it was currently evaluating other power plant proposals in several countries.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65 8703080) =</p>
